# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The plan symbols of windows and doors (drawing quality plan, item 12), as
# segments in plan metres. A house of four 300 mm walls round 10 by 8 m and
# an inner wall: a window in the front wall has its frame (outline and jamb
# lines) 114 mm deep on the wall's line, the glass on the frame's middle,
# and a vensterbank inside and a waterslag outside 30 mm past the faces; the
# same window in the inner wall has no sills, and with a window system
# hosted it keeps only the sills. A plan cut above its head draws nothing; a
# window above the cut is dashed. A window down to the floor (its sill
# less than a sill thick) has no sills. On a wall with a base offset the
# sill and head are measured from the storey, as the evaluation's void. A
# double door in the back wall has two jambs, a threshold, two leaves of half the clear width standing open into
# the house, 40 mm thick, and two swings meeting in the middle; a single
# door in the inner wall has no threshold, and its hand and swing settings
# move its hinges and the side it opens to as EN 12519 names them.
import architectural/openings/bim_opening_symbol.dl

function check opening symbols {boolean:condition} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function opening symbols point {cad vector2:pointValue} is at {a 64 bit floating-point number:wantedX} {a 64 bit floating-point number:wantedY}:
    execute:
        return ((the absolute value of (pointValue's x - wantedX)) < 0.000001) and ((the absolute value of (pointValue's y - wantedY)) < 0.000001)

# Whether `pairs` holds the segment between the two points, either way round.
function opening symbols {a pointer to a list:pairs} hold from {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:bx} {a 64 bit floating-point number:by}:
    execute:
        set held to false
        set pairCursor to 0
        loop while (pairCursor + 1) < (the length of pairs):
            set startPoint to the item at pairCursor in pairs
            set endPoint to the item at (pairCursor + 1) in pairs
            set forward to (opening symbols point startPoint is at ax ay) and (opening symbols point endPoint is at bx by)
            set backward to (opening symbols point startPoint is at bx by) and (opening symbols point endPoint is at ax ay)
            if forward or backward:
                set held to true
            set pairCursor to pairCursor + 2
        return held

# The number of segments in `pairs`.
function the opening symbols count of {a pointer to a list:pairs}:
    execute:
        return (the length of pairs) / 2

# Opening `openingId`'s record in `modelValue`.
function the opening symbols opening {a 64 bit integer:openingId} in {bim model record:modelValue}:
    execute:
        return the item at (the bim opening index of openingId in modelValue)'s position in (modelValue's openings's values)

set modelValue to an empty bim model
set target to the address of modelValue
set ground to add bim level named (the string form of "Ground") at 0.0 with height 3.0 to target
set layerValues to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "brick", 0.3)) to layerValues
set brickType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Brick 300") with layerValues to target
# Counterclockwise, so that each wall's exterior side faces out.
set frontWall to add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 0.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 8.0) to target
set backWall to add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 8.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to target
set innerWall to add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 6.5 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.5 and y 8.0) to target

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the window
# 1200 by 1500 on a 900 sill with a 50 mm frame: a rough opening 1300 wide,
# its head at 2450, centred 2.5 m along the front wall (x 1.85 to 3.15).
set windowType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window 1200") sized 1.2 by 1.5 with sill 0.9 and frame 0.05 to target
set windowId to add bim opening typed windowType in frontWall at 2.5 to target
set windowValue to the opening symbols opening windowId in modelValue
set windowSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening windowValue in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
set windowLines to windowSymbol's lines's values
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of windowLines) = 12) and ((the opening symbols count of (windowSymbol's glazing's values)) = 1)) named (the string form of "a cut window draws twelve lines and one glass line")
check opening symbols (((the length of (windowSymbol's swings's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (windowSymbol's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "a window has no swing and nothing dashed")
check opening symbols (opening symbols (windowSymbol's glazing's values) hold from 1.9 0.0 to 3.1 0.0) named (the string form of "the glass runs between the jambs on the frame's middle, the wall's line")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 0.057 to 3.15 0.057) and (opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 (0.0 - 0.057) to 3.15 (0.0 - 0.057))) named (the string form of "the frame's faces stand 57 mm either side of the line: 114 mm deep")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 (0.0 - 0.057) to 1.85 0.057) and (opening symbols windowLines hold from 3.15 (0.0 - 0.057) to 3.15 0.057)) named (the string form of "the frame's outline closes at the rough opening's ends")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.9 (0.0 - 0.057) to 1.9 0.057) and (opening symbols windowLines hold from 3.1 (0.0 - 0.057) to 3.1 0.057)) named (the string form of "the jambs' inner lines stand the frame width (50 mm) in")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 0.18 to 3.15 0.18) and ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 0.15 to 1.85 0.18) and (opening symbols windowLines hold from 3.15 0.15 to 3.15 0.18))) named (the string form of "the vensterbank stands 30 mm into the house past the inner face")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 (0.0 - 0.18) to 3.15 (0.0 - 0.18)) and ((opening symbols windowLines hold from 1.85 (0.0 - 0.15) to 1.85 (0.0 - 0.18)) and (opening symbols windowLines hold from 3.15 (0.0 - 0.15) to 3.15 (0.0 - 0.18)))) named (the string form of "the waterslag stands 30 mm out past the outer face")
set highCut to the bim plan symbol of opening windowValue in modelValue cut at 2.5 framed true
check opening symbols ((((the length of (highCut's lines's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (highCut's glazing's values)) = 0)) and ((the length of (highCut's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "cut above its head, the window lies in the cut wall and draws nothing")
set hostedSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening windowValue in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed false
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of (hostedSymbol's lines's values)) = 6) and ((the length of (hostedSymbol's glazing's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "with a window system drawing its own frame, only the sills remain")
set innerWindowId to add bim opening typed windowType in innerWall at 1.5 to target
set innerWindow to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening innerWindowId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of (innerWindow's lines's values)) = 6) and ((the opening symbols count of (innerWindow's glazing's values)) = 1)) named (the string form of "a window in an inner wall has its frame and glass but no sills")
set highType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "High window") sized 0.6 by 0.4 with sill 2.2 and frame 0.05 to target
set highId to add bim opening typed highType in frontWall at 5.0 to target
set highSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening highId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols ((((the opening symbols count of (highSymbol's hidden's values)) = 5) and ((the length of (highSymbol's lines's values)) = 0)) and ((the length of (highSymbol's glazing's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "a window wholly above the cut is its frame's outline and middle line, dashed")
check opening symbols (opening symbols (highSymbol's hidden's values) hold from 4.7 0.0 to 5.3 0.0) named (the string form of "its dashed middle line runs between its jambs")
# A window down to the floor (sill 0, 600 wide: x 7.65 to 8.35 on the
# front wall) has its frame and glass but no sills, as its section; so has
# one on a 20 mm sill, less than a sill thick; on a 30 mm sill it has them.
set floorType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window to the floor") sized 0.6 by 2.1 with sill 0.0 and frame 0.05 to target
set floorId to add bim opening typed floorType in frontWall at 8.0 to target
set floorSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening floorId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols ((((the opening symbols count of (floorSymbol's lines's values)) = 6) and ((the opening symbols count of (floorSymbol's glazing's values)) = 1)) and ((opening symbols (floorSymbol's lines's values) hold from 7.65 0.18 to 8.35 0.18) = false)) named (the string form of "a window down to the floor has its frame and glass but no sills")
set lowSillType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window on 20 mm") sized 0.6 by 2.1 with sill 0.02 and frame 0.05 to target
set lowSillId to add bim opening typed lowSillType in frontWall at 8.0 to target
set lowSillSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening lowSillId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
set sillThickType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window on 30 mm") sized 0.6 by 2.1 with sill 0.03 and frame 0.05 to target
set sillThickId to add bim opening typed sillThickType in frontWall at 8.0 to target
set sillThickSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening sillThickId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of (lowSillSymbol's lines's values)) = 6) and ((the opening symbols count of (sillThickSymbol's lines's values)) = 12)) named (the string form of "a 20 mm sill gets no sills, a 30 mm sill (a sill thick) gets both")
set floorHosted to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening floorId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed false
check opening symbols ((((the length of (floorHosted's lines's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (floorHosted's glazing's values)) = 0)) and ((the length of (floorHosted's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "with a window system hosted, a window down to the floor draws nothing of its own")

# ------------------------------------------------------------ base offset
# On a storey at 3 m, a wall standing 0.25 m above it with a window on a
# 1.0 m sill, 1.2 m high: the sill and head stand above the storey (1000
# and 2250), as the evaluation cuts the void and IFC places it, not above
# the wall's base (1250 and 2500). A plan cut 1.2 m above the storey cuts
# it; one cut at 2.3 m lies above its head.
set upperLevel to add bim level named (the string form of "First floor") at 3.0 with height 3.0 to target
set raisedWallId to add bim wall typed brickType on upperLevel from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 0.0) to target
set raisedFound to the bim wall index of raisedWallId in modelValue
set raisedWall to the item at raisedFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set raisedWall's baseOffset to 0.25
replace item at index raisedFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values) with raisedWall
set raisedType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window on 1000") sized 1.2 by 1.2 with sill 1.0 and frame 0.05 to target
set raisedId to add bim opening typed raisedType in raisedWallId at 2.5 to target
set raisedSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening raisedId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols ((((the opening symbols count of (raisedSymbol's lines's values)) = 12) and ((the opening symbols count of (raisedSymbol's glazing's values)) = 1)) and ((the length of (raisedSymbol's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "base offset: a window on a 1.0 m sill is cut 1.2 m above the storey, not dashed")
set raisedHigh to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening raisedId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 2.3 framed true
check opening symbols ((((the length of (raisedHigh's lines's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (raisedHigh's glazing's values)) = 0)) and ((the length of (raisedHigh's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "base offset: cut at 2.3 m, above its 2.25 m head, it draws nothing")

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the double door
# Two leaves of 780 in a 67 mm frame: a rough opening of 1694 centred 2 m
# along the back wall, which runs from x 10 to 0 (x 8.847 to 7.153).
set doubleType to add bim door type named (the string form of "Deur") sized 1.56 by 2.115 with frame 0.067 to target
set bim setting (bim door leaves setting) of doubleType to (2 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
set doubleId to add bim opening typed doubleType in backWall at 2.0 to target
set doubleSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening doubleId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
set doubleLines to doubleSymbol's lines's values
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of doubleLines) = 18) and ((the opening symbols count of (doubleSymbol's swings's values)) = 24)) named (the string form of "a double door draws two jambs, a threshold and two leaves (18 lines) and two swings (24)")
check opening symbols (((the length of (doubleSymbol's glazing's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (doubleSymbol's hidden's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "a door has no glass line and nothing dashed")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols doubleLines hold from 8.847 7.943 to 8.847 8.057) and (opening symbols doubleLines hold from 7.153 7.943 to 7.153 8.057)) named (the string form of "the jambs stand at the rough opening's ends")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols doubleLines hold from 8.78 8.057 to 7.22 8.057) and (opening symbols doubleLines hold from 8.78 7.943 to 7.22 7.943)) named (the string form of "on the outer wall a threshold spans the clear width between the jambs")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols doubleLines hold from 8.78 7.943 to 8.78 7.163) and (opening symbols doubleLines hold from 7.22 7.943 to 7.22 7.163)) named (the string form of "each leaf is hinged at a jamb and stands open 780 mm into the house")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols doubleLines hold from 8.78 7.163 to 8.74 7.163) and (opening symbols doubleLines hold from 7.22 7.163 to 7.26 7.163)) named (the string form of "each leaf is 40 mm thick")
set doubleSwings to doubleSymbol's swings's values
check opening symbols ((opening symbols point (the item at 0 in doubleSwings) is at 8.78 7.163) and (opening symbols point (the item at 23 in doubleSwings) is at 8.0 7.943)) named (the string form of "the first swing runs from its leaf's tip to the middle")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols point (the item at 24 in doubleSwings) is at 7.22 7.163) and (opening symbols point (the item at 47 in doubleSwings) is at 8.0 7.943)) named (the string form of "the second swing meets it in the middle")

# ------------------------------------------------------------ hand and swing
# 930 in a 54 mm frame, 4 m along the inner wall from y 0 to 8: a rough
# opening of 1038 (y 3.481 to 4.519), the wall's exterior side toward +x.
set singleType to add bim door type named (the string form of "Deur") sized 0.93 by 2.315 with frame 0.054 to target
set singleId to add bim opening typed singleType in innerWall at 4.0 to target
set singleSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening singleId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols (((the opening symbols count of (singleSymbol's lines's values)) = 12) and ((the opening symbols count of (singleSymbol's swings's values)) = 12)) named (the string form of "a door in an inner wall has no threshold: two jambs and one leaf (12 lines), one swing")
check opening symbols ((opening symbols (singleSymbol's lines's values) hold from 6.443 4.465 to 5.513 4.465) and (opening symbols point (the item at 23 in (singleSymbol's swings's values)) is at 6.443 3.535)) named (the string form of "left-handed, opening to the interior side (-x): hinged at the +y jamb, its 930 mm leaf shutting toward -y")
set bim setting (bim door hand setting) of singleId to (1 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
set rightSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening singleId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols ((opening symbols (rightSymbol's lines's values) hold from 6.443 3.535 to 5.513 3.535) and (opening symbols point (the item at 23 in (rightSymbol's swings's values)) is at 6.443 4.465)) named (the string form of "right-handed: hinged at the -y jamb instead")
set bim setting (bim door hand setting) of singleId to (0 as a 64 bit integer) keeping false in target
set bim setting (bim door swing setting) of singleId to (1 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
set outwardSymbol to the bim plan symbol of opening (the opening symbols opening singleId in modelValue) in modelValue cut at 1.2 framed true
check opening symbols (opening symbols (outwardSymbol's lines's values) hold from 6.557 3.535 to 7.487 3.535) named (the string form of "left-handed opening to the other side (+x): hinged on that face at the -y jamb")
check opening symbols ((bim door singleId opens outward in modelValue) and ((bim door singleId is right handed in modelValue) = false)) named (the string form of "the settings read back as outward and left-handed")
